-defense</td><td>73,357</td><td>27,736</td><td>35,003</td><td>49,265</td><td>37,321</td><td>31,170</td><td>39,594</td><td>38,994</td><td>30,656</td><td>42,856</td><td>48,267</td><td>42,099</td><td>52,661</td><td>475,619</td><td>451,785</td></tr><tr><td>Grand total</td><td>86,833</td><td>39,968</td><td>48,104</td><td>61,140</td><td>48,963</td><td>40,888</td><td>51,086</td><td>50,642</td><td>40,811</td><td>53,244</td><td>60,073</td><td>51,940</td><td>67,098</td><td>613,958</td><td>580,491</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [231, 1516, 440, 1545], \"page_id\": 23}], \"content\": \"* Less than $500,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [227, 113, 268, 149], \"page_id\": 24}], \"content\": \"16\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1328, 93, 1647, 141], \"page_id\": 24}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [685, 165, 1168, 193], \"page_id\": 24}], \"content\": \"ACCOUNT OF THE U.S. TREASURY\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [458, 273, 1393, 316], \"page_id\": 24}], \"content\": \"Source and Availability of the Balance in the Account of the U.S. Treasury\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [299, 399, 882, 540], \"page_id\": 24}], \"content\": \"The operating cash of the Treasury is maintained in Treasury's accounts with the Federal Reserve banks and branches and in tax loan accounts. As the balances in the accounts at the Federal Reserve Banks become depleted, they are restored by calling in (Withdrawing) funds from thousands of financial institutions throughout the country authorized to maintain tax and loan accounts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [305, 561, 878, 787], \"page_id\": 24}], \"content\": \"Under authority of P.L. 95-147, the Treasury implemented a program on November 2, 1978, to invest a portion of its operating cash in obligations of depositaries maintaining tax and loan accounts. Under the Treasury Tax and Loan investment program, depository financial institutions select the manner in which they will participate in the program. Depositaries that wish to retain funds deposited in their tax and loan accounts in interest-bearing obligations participate under the Note Option; depositaries that wish to remit the funds to the Treasury's account at Federal Reserve banks participate under the Remittance Option.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [966, 404, 1545, 635], \"page_id\": 24}], \"content\": \"Deposits to tax and loan accounts occur in the normal course of business under a uniform procedure applicable to all financial institutions whereby customers of financial institutions deposit with them tax payments and funds for the purchase of Government securities. In most cases the transaction involves merely the transfer of funds from a customer's account to thetax and loan account in the same financial institution. On occasions, to the extent authorized by the Treasury, financial institutions are permitted to deposit in these accounts proceeds from subscriptions to public debt securities entered for their own account as well as for the accounts of their customers.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [957, 645, 1540, 782], \"page_id\": 24}], \"content\": \"The tax and loan system permits the Treasury to collect funds through financial institutions and to leave the funds in Note Option depositaries and in the financial communities in which they arise until such time at the Treasury needs the funds for its operations. In this way the Treasury is able to neutralize the effect of its fluctuation operations on Note Option financial institution reserves and the economy.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [569, 890, 1256, 926], \"page_id\": 24}], \"content\": \"Table UST-1. - Status of the Account of the U.S. Treasury\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [796, 954, 1023, 980], \"page_id\": 24}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [182, 982, 1661, 1746], \"page_id\": 24}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">End of fiscal year or month</th><th colspan=\\\"3\\\">Treasury operating balance 1/ Available funds in demand accounts at:</th><th colspan=\\\"2\\\">Funds in process of collection through</th><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Time deposits and other interest-bearing demand accounts</th><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Other demand accounts 5/</th><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Coin currency and coinage metal</th><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Miscellaneous items</th><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Gold balance 6/</th><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Balance in account of the U.S. Treasury</th></tr><tr><th>Federal Reserve banks</th><th>Treasury tax and loan note accounts</th><th>Other deposits 2/</th><th>Total 3/</th><th>Federal Reserve</th><th>Other depositories 4/</th></tr><tr><td>1971</td><td>1,274</td><td>7,372</td><td>-</td><td>8,755</td><td>419</td><td>-</td><td>187</td><td>-</td><td>441</td><td>108</td><td>109</td><td>9,911</td></tr><tr><td>1972</td><td>2,344</td><td>7,634</td><td>139</td><td>10,117</td><td>252</td><td>179</td><td>54</td><td>-</td><td>471</td><td>129</td><td>107</td><td>11,310</td></tr><tr><td>1973</td><td>4,038</td><td>8,433</td><td>106</td><td>12,576</td><td>243</td><td>117</td><td>41</td><td>-</td><td>586</td><td>70</td><td>107</td><td>13,741</td></tr><tr><td>1974</td><td>2,919</td><td>6,152</td><td>88</td><td>9,159</td><td>276</td><td>135</td><td>19</td><td>-</td><td>602</td><td>54</td><td>106</td><td>10,352</td></tr><tr><td>1975<