": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [968, 1570, 1217, 1618], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"FORRIGN CURRENCY POSITIONS SUMMARY POSITIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [748, 1621, 1439, 2057], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>FCP-I-1.</td><td>Nonbanking firms' positions</td><td>106</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-I-2.</td><td>Weekly bank positions</td><td>106</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-I-3.</td><td>Monthly bank positions</td><td>106</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"3\\\">CANADIAN DOLLAR POSITIONS</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-II-1.</td><td>Nonbanking firms' positions</td><td>107</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-II-2.</td><td>Weekly bank positions</td><td>107</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-II-3.</td><td>Consolidated monthly bank positions</td><td>108</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"3\\\">FRENCH FRANC POSITIONS</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-III-1.</td><td>Nonbanking firms' positions</td><td>109</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-III-2.</td><td>Weekly bank positions</td><td>109</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-III-3.</td><td>Consolidated monthly bank positions</td><td>110</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"3\\\">GERMAN MARK POSITIONS</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-IV-1.</td><td>Nonbanking firms' positions</td><td>111</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-IV-2.</td><td>Weekly bank positions</td><td>111</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-IV-3.</td><td>Consolidated monthly bank positions</td><td>112</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"3\\\">ITALIAN LIRA POSITIONS</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-V-1.</td><td>Nonbanking firms' positions</td><td>113</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1308, 2067, 1338, 2099], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"I\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [151, 55, 196, 104], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"II\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1295, 48, 1586, 96], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [800, 130, 931, 152], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"CONTENTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [155, 198, 1589, 480], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Page</th><th>Page</th></tr><tr><td>FCP-V-2. - Weekly bank positions.................................... 113</td><td>FCP-VIII-2. - Weekly bank positions............................. 119</td></tr><tr><td>JAPANESE YEN POSITIONS</td><td>FCP-VIII-3. - Consolidated monthly bank positions................ 119</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-VI-1. - Nonbanking firms' positions............................ 114</td><td>UNITED STATES DOLLAR POSITIONS ABROAD</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-VI-2. - Weekly bank positions.................................... 114</td><td>FCP-IX-1. - Nonbanking firms' foreign subsidiaries' positions...... 120</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-VI-3. - Consolidated monthly bank positions..................... 115</td><td>FCP-IX-2. - Weekly bank foreign office positions.................. 120</td></tr><tr><td>SWISS FRANC POSITIONS</td><td>FCP-IX-3. - Monthly bank foreign office positions.................. 121</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-VII-1. - Nonbanking firms' positions............................ 116</td><td colspan=\\\"2\\\">FINANCIAL OPERATIONS OF GOVERNMENT AGENCIES AND FUNDS</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-VII-2. - Weekly bank positions................................. 116</td><td colspan=\\\"2\\\">FEDERAL CREDIT PROGRAMS</td></tr><tr><td>FCP-VII-3. - Consolidated monthly bank positions..................... 117</td><td>GA-II-1. - Direct sales and repurchases of loans.................. 123</td></tr><tr><td>STERLING POSITIONS</td><td>Cumulative table of contents.................................... 124</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [156, 487, 822, 511], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"PCP-VIII-1. - Nonbanking firms' positions 118\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [11, 54, 263, 95], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"February 1982\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1411, 56, 1457, 85], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"III\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [501, 115, 972, 134], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [0, 176, 204, 200], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [0, 214, 705, 388], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"On January 13 the Treasury announced that it would auction $5,250 million of 2-year notes to refund $3,994 million of notes maturing January 31, 1982, and to raise $1,256 million new cash. The notes offered were Treasury Notes of Series N-1984, to be dated February 1, 1982, due January 31, 1984, with interest payable on July 31 and January 31 in each year until maturity. A coupon rate of 15% was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [0, 405, 705, 634], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes were received until 1:30 p.m., EST, January 20 and totaled $12,018 million, of which $5,252 million was accepted at yields ranging from 14.95%, price 100.084, up to 15.11%, price 99.816. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield of accepted tenders, 15.08%, price 99.866. These totaled $1,397 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $3,330 million. The $5,252 million of accepted tenders also included $525 million at the average price from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities in exchange for maturing securities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [0, 646, 705, 795], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $5,252 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $490 million of tenders were accepted at the average price from Government accounts and Federal Reserve banks for their own account in exchange for maturing securities, and $302 million of tenders were accepted at the average price from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities for new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [0, 804, 704, 907], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"Tenders were received at Federal Reserve banks and branches and at the Bureau of the Public Debt, Washington, D.C. Bearer and registered notes were authorized to be issued in denominations of $5,000, $10,000, $100,000, and $1,000,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [4, 938, 243, 960], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"February Quarterly Financing\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [5, 970, 712, 1126], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"On January 27 the Treasury announced that it would sell to the public at auction, under competitive and noncompetitive bidding, up to $5,000 million of 3-year notes of Series L-1985, $2,500 million of 10-year notes of Series A-1992, and $2,000 million of 29-3/4-year 147 bonds of 2006-11 to refund $4,320 million of publicly-held Treasury securities maturing February 15, and to raise $5,700 million new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [0, 1138, 707, 1238], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"A coupon rate of 14-5/8% was set on the notes of Series L-1985 after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis. The notes of Series L-1985 will be dated February 16, 1982, due February 15, 1985, with interest payable semiannually on August 15 and February 15 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [0, 1246, 704, 1482], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes of Series L-1985 were received until 1:30 p.m., EST, February 2, and totaled $10,516 million, of which $5,005 million was accepted and yields ranging from 14.57%, price 100.130, up to 14.67%, price 99.894. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield of accepted tenders, 14.63%, price 99.988. These totaled $1,353 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $3,474 million. In addition, $178 million of the notes were allotted at the average price to Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities in exchange for maturing securities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [4, 1487, 707, 1648], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $5,005 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $275 million of tenders were accepted at the average price from Government accounts and Federal Reserve banks for their own account in exchange for maturing securities, and $527 million of tenders were accepted at the average price from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities for new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [2, 1653, 711, 1760], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"A coupon rate of 14-5/8% was set on the notes of Series A-1992 after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis. The notes of Series A-1992 will be dated February 16, 1982, due February 15, 1992, with interest payable semiannually on August 15 and February 15 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [0, 1767, 709, 1923], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the notes of Series A-1992 were received until 1:30 p.m., EST, February 3, and totaled $6,344 million, of which $2,500 million was accepted at yields ranging from 14.60%, price 100.129, up to 14.72%, price 99.51%. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield of accepted tenders, 14.68%, price 99.716. These totaled $417 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $2,083 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [0, 1928, 711, 2082], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $2,500 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $100 million of tenders were accepted at the average price from Government accounts and Federal Reserve banks for their own account in exchange for maturing securities, and $200 million of tenders were accepted at the average price from Federal Reserve banks as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities for new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [759, 176, 1464, 278], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"The 14% bonds of 2006-11 will be an additional issue of the bonds dated November 16, 1981, due November 15, 2011, with interest payable semiannually on May 15 and November 15 until maturity. Prior to the reopening, the public held $1,987 million of the outstanding 14% bonds.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [757, 283, 1464, 441], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"Tenders for the bonds were received until 1:30 p.m., EST, February 4 and totaled $5,050 million, of which $2,500 million was accepted at prices ranging from 96.68, yield 14.47%, down to 95.75, yield 14.61%. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average price of accepted tenders, 96.08, yield 14.56%. These totaled $394 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $2,106 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [759, 446, 1464, 551], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $2,500 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, $75 million of tenders were accepted at the average price from Government accounts and Federal Reserve banks for their own account in exchange for maturing securities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [757, 558, 1468, 641], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"Payment for accepted tenders in all three auctions was required to be completed on or before February 16, 1982, in cash, maturing securities, or other funds immediately available to the Treasury.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [755, 648, 1469, 804], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"Tenders were received in all of the auctions at Federal Reserve banks and branches and at the Bureau of the Public Debt, Washington, D.C. Bearer and registered notes and bonds were authorized to be issued in denominations of $1,000, $5,000, $10,000, $100,000, and $1,000,000 for the issues of 10-year notes and bonds, and $5,000, $10,000, $100,000, and $1,000,000 for the issue of 3-year notes.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [755, 831, 887, 858], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"52-Week Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [755, 860, 1471, 1102], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"On January 21 tenders were invited for approximately $5,250 million of 364-day Treasury bills to be dated January 29, 1982, and to mature January 27, 1983. The issue was to refund $4,684 million of 364-day bills maturing January 28 and raise about $575 million new cash. Tenders were opened on January 21. They totaled $10,446 million, of which $5,251 million was accepted, including $537 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public and $1,125 million of the bills issued at the average price to Federal Reserve banks for themselves and as agents for foreign and international monetary authorities. The average bank discount rate was 13.143%.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [759, 1126, 984, 1153], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"13-Week and 26-Week Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 23, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [762, 1160, 1475, 1348], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"Issues of regular weekly Treasury bills in January totaled $39,400 million. These issues were to refund bills maturing in the amount of approximately $34,825 million and to raise about $4,575 million new cash. In the 13-week series, there were three issues of $4,900 million and one issue of $5,000 million. In the 26-week series, there were three issues of $4,900 million and one issue of $5,000 million. Average rates for the new issues are shown in the following table.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 24, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [757, 1394, 1469, 1628], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Date of issue</th><th colspan=\\\"2\\\">Annual average rate (bank discount basis)</th></tr><tr><th>1982</th><th>13-week</th><th>26-week</th></tr><tr><td>January 7</td><td>11.658</td><td>12.282</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>12.121</td><td>12.806</td></tr><tr><td>21</td><td>12.505</td><td>13.102</td></tr><tr><td>28</td><td>13.364</td><td>13.530</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 25, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [760, 1640, 1281, 1672], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bills (Other than Cash Management Bills) - General\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 26, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [760, 1677, 1473, 1806], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"Treasury bills are sold on a discount basis under competitive and noncompetitive bidding, and at maturity their par amount is payable without interest. All series are issued entirely in book-entry form in a minimum amount of $10,000 and in any higher $5,000 multiple, on the records either of the Federal Reserve banks and branches, or of the Department of the Treasury.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 27, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [760, 1814, 1475, 2082], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"Tenders are received at Federal Reserve banks and branches and from individuals at the Bureau of the Public Debt, Washington. Each tender must be for a minimum of $10,000. Tenders over $10,000 must he in multiples of $5,000. Payment for the full par amount applied for must accompany all tenders submitted for bills to be maintained on the book-entry records of the Department of the Treasury. A cash adjustment will be made for the difference between the par payment submitted and the actual issue price as determined in the auction. No deposit need accompany tenders from incorporated banks and trust companies and from responsible and recognized dealers in investment securities for bills to be maintained on the book-entry records of Federal Reserve banks and branches.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 28, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [122, 55, 165, 99], \"page_id\": 14}], \"content\": \"IV\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1286, 65, 1573, 106], \"page_id\": 14}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [613, 125, 1082, 145], \"page_id\": 14}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [115, 190, 811, 260], \"page_id\": 14}], \"content\": \"deposit of 2 percent of the par amount of the bills applied for must accompany tenders for such bills from others, unless an express guaranty of payment by an incorporated bank or trust company accompanies the tenders.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [117, 277, 811, 369], \"page_id\": 14}], \"content\": \"Noncompetitive tenders (without stated price), usually for $500,000 or less from any one bidder, for each issue of 13-week, 26-week, and 52-week bills, are accepted in full at the weighted average price of accepted competitive bids for an issue.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [119, 388, 809, 429], \"page_id\": 14}], \"content\": \"Payment for accepted tenders must be made or completed on the date of issue in cash or other immediately available funds or in s like par amount of Treasury\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [872, 190, 1570, 231], \"page_id\": 14}], \"content\": \"securities maturing on or before that date. Payment for 13-week, 26-week, and 52-week bills may not be made by credit in Treasury tax and loan accounts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [874, 268, 1397, 280], \"page_id\": 14}], \"content\": \"Nonmarketable Foreign Series Securities - Foreign Governments\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [872, 301, 1571, 417], \"page_id\": 14}], \"content\": \"Dollar-denominated foreign series securities issued to official institutions in January totaled $507 million, consisting of four bills. Redemptions during the month totaled $612 million. At the end of January, dollar-denominated foreign series securities outstanding totaled $14,839 million. (Details are shown on page 43.)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [36, 51, 293, 93], \"page_id\": 15}], \"content\": \"February 1982\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1373, 51, 1398, 83], \"page_id\": 15}], \"content\": \"1\", \"description\": null, \"id