ic Law 93-110, an amendment to the Par Value Modification Act of September 21, 1973, and implementing Treasury regulations. Statistics on the positions have been published monthly since March 1977 beginning with data for December 1975.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [105, 520, 735, 708], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"The report forms and instructions used in the collection of bank data were revised effective with reports as of November 1, 1978, for the weekly reports, and as of October 31, 1978 (the last business day of the month), for the monthly reports. The most recent revision of the nonbank foreign currency forms (see below) became effective as of the last business day of September 1978. Among the changes on the forms, the Belgian franc was deleted as a reporting currency.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [103, 725, 384, 766], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"Common Definitions and Concepts\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [96, 768, 733, 918], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"The term \\\"United States\\\" means the States of the United States, the District of Columbia, the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico, American Samoa, the Canal Zone, Midway Island, the Virgin Islands, and Wake Island. The term \\\"foreign\\\" means locations other than the \\\"United States.\\\" The term \\\"worldwide\\\" is used to describe the sum of \\\"United States\\\" and \\\"foreign\\\" data.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [109, 932, 735, 1110], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"Data for the United States include amounts reported by sole proprietorships, partnerships, and corporations in the United States including the U.S. branches and subsidiaries of foreign nonbanking concerns, in the case of \\\"nonbanking firms' positions,\\\" and the agencies, branches, and subsidiaries located in the United States of foreign banks and banking institutions, in the case of the weekly and monthly \\\"bank positions.\\\"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [107, 1118, 736, 1303], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"Data for \\\"foreign branches\\\" and \\\"abroad\\\" include amounts reported by the branches, majority-owned partnerships and majority-owned subsidiaries of U.S. banking and nonbanking concerns. In general, these data do not reflect the positions of foreign parents or foreign parents' subsidiaries located abroad except through intercompany accounts. The data include the foreign subsidiaries of a few foreign-owned U.S.-based corporations.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [109, 1310, 735, 1392], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"Assets, liabilities, and foreign exchange contract data are reported on the basis of time remaining to maturity as of the date of the report, regardless of the original maturity of the instrument\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [789, 224, 1420, 299], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"involved. \\\"Spot\\\" means due for receipt or delivery within 2 business days from the date of the report. \\\"Short-term\\\" means maturing in 1 year or less from the date of the report.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [789, 303, 1420, 549], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"\\\"Majority-owned foreign partnerships\\\" are those organized under the laws of a foreign country in which one or more nonbanking concerns or nonprofit institutions in the United States, directly or indirectly, own more than 50 percent profit interest. \\\"Majority-owned foreign subsidiaries\\\" are foreign corporations in which one or more nonbanking business concerns or nonprofit institutions located in the United States directly or indirectly own stock with more than 50 percent of the total combined voting power of all classes of stock entitled to vote, or more than 50 percent of the total value of all classes of stock.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [793, 566, 973, 592], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"Reporting Threshold\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [794, 595, 1424, 836], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"The exemption level applicable to banks and banking institutions is $10 million equivalent. The exemption level applicable to nonbanking business concerns and nonprofit institutions was $1 million equivalent on all nonbank forms from March 1975 through November 1976. It was raised to $2 million equivalent on the monthly reports of positions held in the United States. From November 1976 through September 1978 the exemption level was raised to $3 million on foreign subsidiary positions on June 31, 1977, and for positions held in the United States on September 30, 1978.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [794, 838, 1427, 1156], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"Firms must report their entire foreign currency position in a specified foreign currency if a specified U.S. dollar equivalent value is reached in any category of assets, liabilities, exchange contracts bought and sold, or the net position in the currency. In general, exemption levels are applied to the entire firm in the United States and separately to each foreign branch or subsidiary. In reports on their foreign branches, majority-owned foreign partnerships and majority-owned foreign subsidiaries, U.S. banks and nonbanks are required to report the U.S. dollar-denominated assets, liabilities, exchange contracts bought and sold, and net positions of those branches, partnerships, and subsidiaries with reportable positions in the specified foreign currencies.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [796, 1175, 1029, 1204], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"Description of Statistics\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [794, 1211, 1425, 1404], \"page_id\": 119}], \"content\": \"Data collected on the Treasury foreign currency forms are published in the Treasury Bulletin in nine sections. The first section presents a summary of worldwide net positions in all of the currencies reported. Sections II through VIII each present data on a Specified foreign currency. Section IX presents the U.S. dollar positions of the foreign branches and subsidiaries of U.S. firms which are required to report in one or more of the specified foreign currencies.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 22, 237, 53], \"page_id\": 120}], \"content\": \"106\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1208, 17, 1500, 60], \"page_id\": 120}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [645, 91, 1045, 108], \"page_id\": 120}], \"content\": \"FOREIGN CURRENCY POSITIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [645, 131, 1045, 153], \"page_id\": 120}], \"content\": \"Section I - Summary Positions\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [552, 160, 1163, 196], \"page_id\": 120}], \"content\": \"Table FCP-I-1. - Nonbanking Firms' Positions\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [667, 215, 1015, 237], \"page_id\": 120}], \"content\": \"(In millions of foreign currency units)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [177, 232, 1515, 426], \"page_id\": 120}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Report date</th><th>Canadian dollars (1)</th><th>French francs